   "text": "I read the structure as an isavuconazonium-type molecule, a 1,2,4-triazol-4-ium prodrug. I assembled the SMILES region by region and then worked out the two stereocentres from the wedge and hash bonds.\n\n**Regions of the drawing**\n- **Left side chain:** a sarcosine-type ester, CH3-NH-CH2-C(=O)-O-CH2, attached to the 3-position of a pyridine.\n- **Pyridine linkage:** the 2-position of the pyridine carries N(CH3)-C(=O)-O-CH(CH3)-, a carbamate that attaches to the triazolium nitrogen N4\u207a.\n- **Triazolium ring:** five atoms, N1(chain)\u2013CH=N\u207a(substituted)\u2013CH=N\u2013back to N1. The chain on N1 is a CH2 leading to the quaternary carbon.\n- **Quaternary carbon:** it carries OH on a wedge, a 2,5-difluorophenyl group, the CH2 to the triazole, and the CH(CH3) carbon.\n- **CH(CH3) carbon:** its methyl is on a hash, and it carries a thiazol-2-yl group. The thiazole bears a 4-(4-cyanophenyl) substituent.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- **CH(CH3) carbon:** the methyl is hashed, so H points toward the viewer. Taking the neighbours in the order methyl, H, thiazole, quaternary C, this gives `[C@@H]`.\n- **Quaternary carbon:** the OH is wedged. Taking the neighbours in the order CH, O, CH2, aryl, this gives `[C@]`.\n\nThe triazolium carbon bearing the CH(CH3) group is drawn with plain bonds, so it gets no stereo label.\n\nSMILES: C[C@@H](c1nc(-c2ccc(C#N)cc2)cs1)[C@](O)(Cn1c[n+](C(C)OC(=O)N(C)c2ncccc2COC(=O)CNC)cn1)c1cc(F)ccc1F"
